#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""FS3 v196 - 2.5D step 1: capital ships drawn from their 3D models.

    Field      Capital ships with a converted model (the 16 GTVA support
               ships) are drawn from it instead of their sprite: one WebGL
               picture of the field, under the fighters and shots, over the
               backdrop, beams and wreckage. A perspective camera straight
               at the middle of the field, so the ships sit exactly where
               the sprites sat; only the hull's own depth shows. Facing
               left a ship shows her other flank, as a real ship would.
               Hits, mounts, subsystems and the damage logic are unchanged;
               the damage marks lie on the 3D hull. Shivans and NTF reskins
               stay sprites until their models are converted. Without WebGL
               everything is drawn as before.
    Models     A 'full' level for these 16 ships (every part of the finest
               detail level) in models_v196.zip - the field uses it, and the
               previews now do too (Silvio: black patches on the Orion).

Needs v195. Adds src/59_field3d.js, edits src/20_render.js,
src/58_model3d.js, src/70_ui.js and fieldsim.js. Run assemble.py afterwards.
"""
